From 67074eb394d99ff7c280dbf1154082336cc6c867 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 19:17:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kittytk: deliver bracketed paste as a whole PasteEvent, not a
 key flood
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A paste into the TUI host (KittyTK running in a regular terminal) was lost or
truncated: the host never enabled bracketed paste, never wired OnPaste, and had
no route for a paste to reach a focused trinket. So the outer terminal shipped a
paste as a raw byte flood, direct-key-handler surfaced it one key at a time, and
those per-character events overran the 256-slot event queue — whose overflow
branch silently drops. Large pastes lost their tail; nothing arrived as a paste.
Not mew-specific: any focused trinket, a plain PurfecTerm included, saw it.

Fix, every layer:

- backend/tui: enable ?2004h (disable ?2004l on teardown); take paste via
  OnPaste with EmitPasteKeys off so it is not re-echoed as keys; deliver one
  core.PasteEvent per paste through a blocking enqueue that cannot be truncated.
- core: PasteHandler interface, and FocusManager/GlobalFocusManager.HandlePaste
  routing a paste to the focused trinket — mirroring the composition path.
- desktop/window/mdipane: forward PasteEvent down the same container chain as a
  composition (focused trinket only; no shortcut/menu/key fallback).
- trinkets: PurfecTerm.HandlePaste re-brackets for the CHILD per the child's own
  paste mode (raw otherwise), so a paste reaches the inner program — or the mew
  editor, which embeds *PurfecTerm — as a real paste. TextInput.HandlePaste
  inserts at the caret. Paste text on the wire, framing decided at the edge.

Tests cover the backend (one intact PasteEvent, large paste not dropped), focus
routing, and PurfecTerm re-bracketing per inner mode. Bumps the KittyTK build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FSviWi6Z2uUeVwC6CKBApG
